  "claims": [
    "Circle supports Deformable output, Degree 2..11 and bounded PointCount settings through one edit-free wrapper around the existing Circle construction getter.",
    "Periodic non-rational NURBS interpolate equal-angle seam stations for every degree and use domain [0,2*pi]. Even degrees differ from Rebuild half-span collocation. The linear-time circle solve evaluates only the first Fourier harmonic in the shared periodic B-spline basis.",
    "Full command and frontend comparisons cover all controls, weights, knots, domains, lengths, closed status, source geometry, returned selection and actual Undo/Redo on both backends for 57 successful native workflows.",
    "Construction coverage includes center/size, all four size options, tilted points, 2Point, 3Point, 3Point Radius, Vertical, Orientation, AroundCurve guides and preselected FitPoints. Degree/PointCount prompts, defaults, saved settings, relative/CPlane input and exact output reset are measured.",
    "Three acknowledged owned public surface/Brep edge clicks qualify projected AroundCurve construction; existing source and selection/history policies are reused.",
    "Four clean native cancellations at center, size, Degree and PointCount leave no output or history in command and frontend replay.",
    "Native layouts below the measured periodic minimum use a different clamped approximation. Eight clean native examples are retained as excluded diagnostics and are rejected atomically locally. The ordinary Circle getter rejects before the first point and allows PointCount correction in the same session.",
    "Local checks cover preview/commit equality at large world origins, captured construction planes after view changes, registry preference lifetime, postselected FitPoints, shared filters/distance constraints, scalar area input, dense 1000-point station interpolation and guide freshness for exact/deformable output.",
    "All previous Circle and 115 Ellipse native workflows remain regression coverage on both backends. Prior valid provenance hashes are archived to their original baseline Git blobs without changing historical outcomes."
  ],
  "periodic_minimum_unique_points": {
    "2": 4,
    "3": 4,
    "4": 5,
    "5": 6,
    "6": 7,
    "7": 9,
    "8": 10,
    "9": 12,
    "10": 13,
    "11": 15
  },
  "point_count_getter_policy": "Integer Degree+2..1000. Lower periodic layouts can be retained by raising Degree after a valid lower-degree PointCount. Canonical commits preserve that legal ordering.",
  "source_selection_policy": "Compare native after_script as the returned state. Native EndCommand after temporarily highlights a postselected whole guide. Returned/Undo/Redo release that highlight, retain preselection and leave edge parents unselected.",
